 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 534193,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the measure of each interior angle of a regular pentagon and then find the sum of the interior angles.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>A pentagon has five sides, so <span data-math=\"n = 5\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The measure of each interior angle of a regular polygon with <i>n</i> sides is given by <span data-math=\"a = \\frac{{\\left( {n - 2} \\right)180^\\circ }}{n}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"a = \\frac{{\\left( {n - 2} \\right)180^\\circ }}{n} = \\frac{{\\left( {5 - 2} \\right)180^\\circ }}{5} = \\frac{{\\left( 3 \\right)180^\\circ }}{5} = \\frac{{540}}{5} = 108^\\circ \"></span></p>\n<p>The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with <i>n</i> sides is <span data-math=\"S = \\left( {n - 2} \\right)180^\\circ \"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"S = \\left( {n - 2} \\right)180^\\circ = \\left( {5 - 2} \\right)180^\\circ = \\left( 3 \\right)180^\\circ = 540^\\circ \"></span></p>\n<p>Each interior angle of a pentagon is 108°. The sum of the interior angles of a pentagon is 540°.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"a = {108^ \\circ }\">a = {108^ \\circ }</span>\n<br>\nThe sum of the interior angles is <span data-math=\"{540^ \\circ }\">{540^ \\circ }</span>."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
